    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Find two fractions between $-\\frac{1}{3}$ and $-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $-\\frac{5}{12}$ and $-\\frac{3}{8}$.",
      "worked": "Write both endpoints with denominator 24:\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{1}{2}&=-\\frac{12}{24}\\\\-\\frac{1}{3}&=-\\frac{8}{24}\\end{align*}$$\nChoose two numerators strictly between $-12$ and $-8$:\n$$-\\frac{12}{24}<-\\frac{10}{24}<-\\frac{9}{24}<-\\frac{8}{24}.$$\nThus two possible fractions are $-\\frac{5}{12}$ and $-\\frac{3}{8}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
